    </joint>
    <gpio name="dxl1">
      <param name="type">dxl</param>
      <param name="ID">11</param>
      <param name="Torque Enable">1</param>
      <param name="Min Position Limit">1650</param>
      <param name="Max Position Limit">2446</param>
      <command_interface name="Goal Current"/>
      <param name="Operating Mode">0</param>
      <param name="Current Limit">500</param>
      <param name="PWM Limit">885</param>
      <state_interface name="Present Position"/>
      <state_interface name="Present Velocity"/>
      <state_interface name="Present Current"/>
      <state_interface name="Torque Enable"/>
      <state_interface name="Present Input Voltage"/>
      <!-- ============ j1 SERVO LOOP - DELIBERATELY SOFT (2026-08-12) =========
             NO COLON-SPACE ANYWHERE BELOW, and no doubled dash either (XML
             forbids that inside a comment at all). This comment survives into
             the generated URDF, and gazebo_ros2_control hands that whole string
             to rcl as a parameter-override rule of the form
             `robot_description:=<urdf>`, whose value is parsed as YAML. A
             single colon followed by a space makes the parser read a mapping
             there, the rule is rejected, and the plugin's controller_manager
             is never created -
             every Gazebo spawner then waits forever on
             /controller_manager/list_controllers. The launch files dodge the
             same trap with ParameterValue(value_type=str); the plugin has no
             such escape hatch, so the rule is absolute here.

             Joint 1 is the arm's special case in position mode - a vertical
             yaw axis carries ZERO gravity preload (nothing pins the gearbox
             to one side of its friction/backlash cone) and the inverted home
             [0,40,40,0] puts ~10x the upright yaw inertia behind it. At the
             stock loop gains the joint has a stable LIMIT CYCLE of 0.53 deg
             pk-pk (+/-3 encoder counts, ~ the gearbox backlash) at a
             gain-invariant 4.2-4.6 Hz. The rest state is also stable - a
             firm nudge (or, on the drone, any disturbance) knocks it into
             the orbit, where it stays. Diagnosed by elimination on the
             bench, one register at a time, live (Key Items item 8, bags
             results/bags/2026-08-12). Every integrator and derivative term
             in the Mode-3 cascade pumps the orbit against stiction
             (position I, velocity I, position D on the late quantized
             velocity estimate), and the remaining P-P loop still sustains
             it at stock stiffness. Torque mode is immune - Mode 0 runs
             none of this cascade, and our PD+ is soft with i_deadband.
             So j1 gets the same philosophy the torque law converged on -
             soft proportional-only, both loops, and nothing that
             integrates or differentiates. It holds nothing against
             gravity, so this costs no accuracy - standing error stays
             under one encoder count.
             These are RAM registers, reset to firmware defaults on every
             power cycle, so values poked by hand DO NOT SURVIVE a relaunch
             (that reversion derailed the diagnosis twice). This block is
             the only place they may be set. j2-j4 keep stock gains -
             gravity preload means they cannot hunt, and their integrators
             close real gravity droop. -->
      <param name="Position P Gain">400</param>
      <param name="Position I Gain">0</param>
      <param name="Position D Gain">0</param>
      <param name="Velocity P Gain">50</param>
      <param name="Velocity I Gain">0</param>
      <param name="Profile Velocity">200</param>
      <param name="Profile Acceleration">50</param>
      <param name="Drive Mode">0</param>
      <param name="Return Delay Time">0</param>
    </gpio>
    <gpio name="dxl2">
      <param name="type">dxl</param>
      <param name="ID">12</param>
      <param name="Torque Enable">1</param>
      <param name="Min Position Limit">1138</param>
      <param name="Max Position Limit">2616</param>
      <command_interface name="Goal Position"/>
      <param name="Operating Mode">3</param>
      <param name="PWM Limit">885</param>
      <state_interface name="Present Position"/>
      <state_interface name="Present Velocity"/>
      <state_interface name="Present Current"/>
      <state_interface name="Torque Enable"/>
      <state_interface name="Present Input Voltage"/>
      <param name="Position P Gain">800</param>
      <param name="Position I Gain">100</param>
      <param name="Position D Gain">100</param>
      <param name="Profile Velocity">200</param>
      <param name="Profile Acceleration">50</param>
